The train’s average speed is found by dividing the distance it travels by the time it takes, and then converting the result to metres per second.

1. **Compute the speed in kilometres per hour**

\[
\text{Speed (km/h)} = \frac{\text{distance (km)}}{\text{time (h)}} 
= \frac{240\ \text{km}}{2.5\ \text{h}} = 96\ \text{km/h}
\]

2. **Convert kilometres per hour to metres per second**

\[
1\ \text{km/h}= \frac{1000\ \text{m}}{3600\ \text{s}} = \frac{5}{18}\ \text{m/s}
\]

